1. SCENARIO OBJECTIVES & INTERLOCK SPECIFICATION
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Objective:
  Simulate and audit the automatic emergency cutoff of the tank discharge pump
  under an extreme low-level dry-run scenario. Protect the mechanical pump asset
  from cavitation, fluid starvation, dry-running mechanical seal friction wear,
  and catastrophic thermal destruction.

Interlock Rules (TankLevelClosedLoop.st, Lines 82-88):
  - TRIP CONDITION  : TankLevelPV <= 10.0%  <==>  %AI1 <= 3200 ADC counts (5.60 mA)
    * Action        : %M10 (AlarmLowLow) := TRUE (1)
    * Action        : %Q1  (PumpRunCmd)  := FALSE (0) [FORCED DE-ENERGIZATION]
    * Response Time : Exactly 1 PLC scan cycle (<= 10.0 milliseconds)

  - RESET CONDITION : TankLevelPV > 12.0%   <==>  %AI1 > 3840 ADC counts (5.92 mA)
    * Deadband      : 2.0% Hysteresis (640 ADC counts) preventing contactor chatter
    * Action        : %M10 (AlarmLowLow) := FALSE (0)
    * Action        : %Q1  (PumpRunCmd)  := TRUE (1) [AUTOMATIC RE-ENERGIZATION]

